{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04XQ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Delta_f$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-representable-locally-separated-diagonal-immersion}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5ed1e00997af5cb6ccf579bf4ff955a8b622fe6aaa0565ef601b357242d6b789", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:93dc5532a6262336f17b5a6650732b5499135e24c0a1caf527fc0995470e5380", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks\nrepresentable by algebraic spaces. Then the following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is locally separated, and\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0003> is an immersion.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:90f84ebcd5de0893d83f7cf658bcb170502a66de339682e2135b0b8165658103", "unit_id": "tag:04YU:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04XQ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Delta_f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-properties-section-properties-morphisms}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-representable-separated-diagonal-closed}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-representable-quasi-separated-diagonal-quasi-compact}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4db9bd067ca49be6b0661008d36d93d7b0798270efc8bda15da301396a0b152e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:25dfb476a2bd0297a063e0aa0c606aa1411f925a999da42ef077454272094688", "source_text": "The statements ``<MATH_0001> is locally separated'', and ``<MATH_0002> is an immersion''\nrefer to the notions defined in\nProperties of Stacks,\nSection <REF_0001>.\nProof omitted. Hint: Argue as in the proofs of\nLemmas <REF_0002> and\n<REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:552ae284f4608eebf3ad48f54e65359241d01fd72e453ed476768fb399186da7", "unit_id": "tag:04YU:proof"}
